{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509436-the-new-sect","id":1509436,"title":"The New Sect","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-23T20:09:14-07:00","id":1509436,"title":"The New Sect","content":"I'm a big fan of the Circulatory System idea. With the Sabbat taking a backseat and the renewed hostility between the Cam and the Anarchs, such a new organization is refreshing and it plays expertly into the new Blood mechanics and it's an option for lower Humanity kin to flourish without going into the fanatical and dogmatic deep end of the Sabbat. Another thing I like about it is its lack of ideology. It's a job, albeit a very demanding one and I view it as an opportunity for outlier Clans to gain a larger foothold and gain power.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla are predominantly: Ventrue, Toreador, Tremere, Malkavian, Nosferatu <br /> The Anarchs: Brujah, Gangrel, Caitiff, Thin-Blood, Ministry<br /> <br /> The System is a chance for underdogs, independents and those with falling stock to enter and flourish: Ravnos, Tremere, Thin-Bloods, Banu Haqim, Hecata (I really like this collection as a bloc, btw)<br /> <br /> Hecata are a no-brainer for leadership duties and the System seems tailor made for their inclusion; I could see a vicious struggle for power by them to seize such an important apparatus. Ravnos are sometimes portrayed as couriers and their natures and skills would serve the System well in regards to transportation and trafficking, whilst giving them a chance to rebuild as a Clan, especially if you dispense with their standard Compulsion and roll with one of the alternatives that exist out there. TB's, Tremere and the BH all have their place in the R&amp;D section of the System and TB's especially have an important role to play that would give them footing in finding a place in the night, with the Banu Haqim serving as the primary martial edge.<br /> <br /> The Circulatory System has tremendous potential and I hope it becomes a fixture in VTM and is significantly expanded upon. I like V5's emphasis on smaller cults as well, but the System feels like just what was needed as an alternative to the current Cam-Anarch dichotomy. <br /> <br /> What are your thoughts on this new pseudo-sect and its potential?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27842-shovelheart3","name":"ShovelHeart3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27842_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T21:00:08-07:00","id":1509439,"title":"","content":"I would expect that the Circulatory System would very much refrain from setting itself up as a rival sect to the Anarchs or Camarilla. In the end, the goal is business. If it sets itself up as a political rival to the Camarilla or Anarchs, then there's a high likelihood that those groups will set up their own &quot;circulatory system&quot; type organizations rather than relying on an explicit rival for something as fundamentally necessary as blood.<br /> <br /> I do think that the Hecata (especially the Giovanni) would be the big players in the Circulatory System and generally the ones in overall control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T21:12:18-07:00","id":1509441,"title":"","content":"How does this work exactly? I mean, the Ravnos are few and far between and you can't have two of them bumping into each other without causing a slaughter, the Tremere and the Banu Haqim hate each other, and the Hecata already mess with the traffic, I can only think that some of the younger ones were displeased. how order is maintained within the clan and decided to disband.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T23:23:14-07:00","id":1509452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509436-the-new-sect?p=1509439#post1509439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would expect that the Circulatory System would very much refrain from setting itself up as a rival sect to the Anarchs or Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I don't think it would want to do that; there's no point. A parallel would be how corporations in the real world work through and influence governments for their power. They use public institutions for tools. If you become another political sect, that advantage is gone and since the CS has no inherent ideology, it would just fracture and the pieces reabsorbed by the parent sects.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the end, the goal is business. If it sets itself up as a political rival to the Camarilla or Anarchs, then there's a high likelihood that those groups will set up their own &quot;circulatory system&quot; type organizations rather than relying on an explicit rival for something as fundamentally necessary as blood. </div> </div> </div>There's really nothing that political to build around. If an Anarch joins, they're just indirectly supporting the society the Cam has built and I doubt they would want to destroy it, either because it's too damn useful. There's no reason to be at odds with the Cam, either because those are your best customers. I think the CS is probably already localized to a degree where it might have more of an Anarch or Camarilla bent depending on where you are, but in all likeliness, you're probably still dealing with the least ideological members of either sect. Also, while the BH and Tremere have their machinations, I think they value their blood and knowledge addictions over being faux-Ventrue or Lasombra. The power of the System is most likely just a means to an end for them. TB's and Ravnos aren't in any position to be making moves, either. Then there's the Hecata, but they have enough internal affairs to tend to keep them busy in the near future. If anything, the CS would probably want to perpetuate conflict between the sects and profit off both sides (like a real corporation).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do think that the Hecata (especially the Giovanni) would be the big players in the Circulatory System and generally the ones in overall control. </div> </div> </div>Absolutely and if there were to be any point of contention, it'd start there. Controlling the CS would be like controlling the vampiric Central Bank, almost.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27832_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27832\" data-vbnamecard=\"27832\">Psicose</a> I don't think the Ravnos still have a problem with each other and the BH and Tremere are both still reeling from their internal schisms, so I doubt they'd be in a position to turn down the advantages of the System, in which they would both greatly benefit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27842-shovelheart3","name":"ShovelHeart3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27842_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T06:34:49-07:00","id":1509474,"title":"","content":"I don't guess the Ravnos could be free of something made from an Antedilluvian so easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T09:02:24-07:00","id":1509483,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of a quasi sect coming into power and appealing to clans who don't fit comfortably with the other sects and I could see the Banu Haqim Vizers and blood magi being interested way more then the warrior caste though I can see them being a strong part of the CS. I'm not so sure about the Tremere though joining this possible sect as they fit better with the Camarilla sect in general and would provide them with way better security to stay with them. But I can see a few of the more rebellious ones joining them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 04-24-2023, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T11:53:46-07:00","id":1509507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509436-the-new-sect?p=1509441#post1509441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I mean, the Ravnos are few and far between and you can't have two of them bumping into each other without causing a slaughter</div> </div> </div> </div>that was only during the week of nightmare. Most of them have figured out since then that they can be in each other presence.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19506-killtron","name":"Killtron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T22:38:08-07:00","id":1509558,"title":"","content":"The carmarilla vs anarch dynamic is actually pretty weak and politics in v5 is hyper localised. so it's difficult to define what this sect would contribute because its pan city status would ensure rapid dominance. I'm unsure why the tremere would get in on this because they have very strong links with the ivory tower.<br /> <br /> I'd remove the tremere and implement the setites instead. I also think this would work better in a Sabbat/carmarilla dynamique or with a major re write of the anarchs.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 04-25-2023, 01:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T09:16:33-07:00","id":1509593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509436-the-new-sect?p=1509558#post1509558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The camarilla vs anarch dynamic is actually pretty weak and politics in v5 is hyper localised</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant in regards to player choice, since the Sabbat isn't really meant to be played in V5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> so it's difficult to define what this sect would contribute because its pan city status would ensure rapid dominance. </div> </div> </div>Well, it's a business, but a very personal business. You will deal with kindred of all types and their diverse needs. I kinda see it as a criminal organization combined with a corporation. There's a lot of potential for intrigue. One influence for me on thinking about the System is the novel/film Fight Club. The search for personal meaning (or lack of it) is influenced by the characters' relationship with society and the system they exist in. There's a lot of potential for individual stories. I strongly recommend the Bloody Awful Business supplement as a starting point:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/397069/Bloody-Awful-Business?term=Bloody+awf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/1/397069.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/397069/Bloody-Awful-Business?term=Bloody+awf\" target=\"_blank\"> Bloody Awful Business - White Wolf | DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/397069/Bloody-Awful-Business?term=Bloody+awf\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/397069/Bloody-Awful-Business?term=Bloody+awf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Bloody Awful Business - Bloody Awful Business: A Kindred&rsquo;s Guide to the Circulatory System is a Player&rsquo;s Guide and Storyteller&rsquo;s Resource </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I also think there's a lot of potential for internal competition within the System and the nature of kindred all but assures this. You wouldn't have the culture of the Camarilla or the Sabbat binding everyone so tightly together.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm unsure why the tremere would get in on this because they have very strong links with the ivory tower.<br /> <br /> I'd remove the tremere and implement the setites instead. I also think this would work better in a Sabbat/carmarilla dynamique or with a major re write of the anarchs. </div> </div> </div>The System is intertwined with the Tower and the Tremere would have an apparatus with vast amounts of resources to pursue their experiments with. They'd also be intimately invested in what the Thin-Bloods are doing. I can't see them not having an interest. I could certainly envision significant Ministry involvement, though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27842-shovelheart3","name":"ShovelHeart3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27842_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T07:25:12-07:00","id":1509718,"title":"","content":"I never really cared for the idea of the &quot;Anarchs&quot; being a sect in of itself but, instead a collection of independent realms that come together to form a collective against outside forces. That classical Empire VS 'City State confederation' that you see in RPGs.<br /> <br /> So in my mind, there should be tons of these groups that make up the entire fabric of the Anarchs. I think is really a much larger issue that VtM as a whole has with their Sect system and the layout of the global stage. I don't really care for the idea of things being either one of two sects and in my personal games I try to inject as much local sects/factions into the mix.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T17:00:37-07:00","id":1509797,"title":"","content":"The concept of a CS being born as a separate (politically or ideologically) organization or sect could be a nice set up for a chronicle, since Sabbat is in decline (&quot;proud to be a vampire&quot; attitude in modern times makes your life shorter). I can easily see a huge influx of Kindred of independent clans working for a common economical, rather than politcal goal. Since they are independent, I see less grudge-based friction. It can even be survival-driven: Hecata going all-in into Blood Bank business to mitigate masquerade-breaching incidents of messy feeding since not all Hecata kindred eat corpses, and blood bags don't scream in pain... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27765-euderos","name":"Euderos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27765_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T09:57:35-07:00","id":1510100,"title":"","content":"I hope at some point you will tell us how successful you were at fleshing out the CS as a quasi sect in your game Shovelheart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 04-29-2023, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T12:04:35-07:00","id":1510117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShovelHeart3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509436-the-new-sect?p=1509593#post1509593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The System is intertwined with the Tower and the Tremere would have an apparatus with vast amounts of resources to pursue their experiments with. They'd also be intimately invested in what the Thin-Bloods are doing. I can't see them not having an interest. I could certainly envision significant Ministry involvement, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>They already have that and the prestige of being one of the big three in the tower. They'd effectively be losing power and security by joining this sect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 04-29-2023, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T14:21:41-07:00","id":1510411,"title":"","content":"Agreed Ragged Robin. The Tremere clan won't leave the Camarilla as that sect benefits them the most and at best you might get a few rebellious ones who might want to join and get on the ground floor and hope for positions of importance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T16:53:52-07:00","id":1510531,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not quite seeing why this would be a new Sect, as an alternative to the Camarilla/Sabbat. Why would someone not be able to be a member of the Camarilla AND the Circulatory System? <br /> Being a member of the Sabbat obviously prevents you being a member of the Camarilla, and vice versa, they\u2019re diametrically opposed philosophies and outlooks on the role of vampires and their way of interacting with the world. Anarchs are defined by their rejection of both these organisations, rather than any unifying characteristics themselves. <br /> <br /> The Circulatory System though\u2026 is a job. It\u2019s not something contradictory to the other Sects. It\u2019s just something a vampire can do to earn influence/boons/money. <br /> I mean, yes it\u2019s a cool concept, but that doesn\u2019t particularly make it another Sect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27967-caerolion","name":"Caerolion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T17:06:03-07:00","id":1510532,"title":"","content":"The CS would be more effective if it remained neutral and spanned all the sects. I think most of us can agree on that. But I think the OP is onto something, as others have spotted: localising things and having a plethora of smaller affiliations (cults, &quot;businesses&quot;, etc) PCs can identify with is definitely something that makes sense and allows for more diverse (and more precarious) &quot;urban sandboxes&quot; in VTM. Especially because such affiliations can cross sects, allowing players to mix Camarilla, Anarch, Sabbat and independent lineages with greater ease, without sacrificing some level of antagonism and paranoia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T16:29:13-07:00","id":1513898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509436-the-new-sect?p=1509718#post1509718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never really cared for the idea of the &quot;Anarchs&quot; being a sect in of itself but, instead a collection of independent realms that come together to form a collective against outside forces. That classical Empire VS 'City State confederation' that you see in RPGs.<br /> <br /> So in my mind, there should be tons of these groups that make up the entire fabric of the Anarchs. I think is really a much larger issue that VtM as a whole has with their Sect system and the layout of the global stage. I don't really care for the idea of things being either one of two sects and in my personal games I try to inject as much local sects/factions into the mix.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I concur. The Anarchs have never been interesting to me and have a distinct lack of culture and identity other than &quot;fuck the Camarilla&quot;. I think V5 did a really good job with emphasizing minor cults and creating a nice tapestry of intrigue at the local level. Honestly, the Anarchs always felt like the designers wanted something besides the Cam-Sab dichotomy, but just came up short of a good idea. If the Sabbat can be pushed into the backseat, I'd really like to see the Anarchs given a conceptual demotion. I think creating subversive factions within the Camarilla itself would be far more intriguing. Because the thing is, neonates are inherently dangerous. They're young and relatively stupid, but powerful and numerous. If anything, a youth movement would be scariest when coming from the ranks of the Tower itself. It'd be a constant struggle between master and apprentice, instead of the typical &quot;you're my bitch, childe&quot;. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27842-shovelheart3","name":"ShovelHeart3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27842_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T18:08:54-07:00","id":1513905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShovelHeart3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509436-the-new-sect?p=1513898#post1513898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I concur. The Anarchs have never been interesting to me and have a distinct lack of culture and identity other than &quot;fuck the Camarilla&quot;. I think V5 did a really good job with emphasizing minor cults and creating a nice tapestry of intrigue at the local level. Honestly, the Anarchs always felt like the designers wanted something besides the Cam-Sab dichotomy, but just came up short of a good idea. If the Sabbat can be pushed into the backseat, I'd really like to see the Anarchs given a conceptual demotion. I think creating subversive factions within the Camarilla itself would be far more intriguing. Because the thing is, neonates are inherently dangerous. They're young and relatively stupid, but powerful and numerous. If anything, a youth movement would be scariest when coming from the ranks of the Tower itself. It'd be a constant struggle between master and apprentice, instead of the typical &quot;you're my bitch, childe&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are actually describing what Anarchs used to be originally in V1, before the Sabbat was even developed beyond the idea of scary boogey people.<br /> It was during later editions, once the Sabbat - Camarilla conflict took central stage, that the War of Ages, one of the central themes of VtM, was pushed aside in favour of the, IMO, less interesting War of Sects. <br /> What is even worse is that now that V5 got rid of the Sabbat, they turned the Anarchs into a Sabbat lite and kept the War of Sects angle, and even finally put an end to the War of Ages by putting the Elders in a bus.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T19:57:58-07:00","id":1513909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509436-the-new-sect?p=1510100#post1510100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope at some point you will tell us how successful you were at fleshing out the CS as a quasi sect in your game Shovelheart.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've taken a little time away from VTM, actually, so I haven't been giving it too much thought. <br /> <br /> Anyway, here are some rudimentary ideas I have about the CS:<br /> <br /> Like I said, it's a pseudo-sect, not a full one and even more individualistic than all the other sects, but there is a little spark of culture there. One idea I had was that the CS has a fight club. It's a place for employees to blow off steam and express their ephemeral moments of nihilism with each other after a hard day's work. <br /> <br /> I also see it as filled with opportunity. I think it would attract a lot of Sabbat defectors who have grown tired of an unlife in Caine's service. There'd also be a lot of scrappy, young Camarilla cubs looking to make a name in a space that the elders don't have a firm grip on, probably from parents who aren't too high up in the Tower; think of them as the lower middle class kids that have to get a job to support themselves. I see it as extremely technologically literate. I see it as a melting pot where desperate Ravnos rub shoulders with ambitious Tzimisce, almost like a micro-America. It's a new land of opportunity and it's all up for grabs. <br /> <br /> I envision it as very close to a criminal organization: robbery, assassination, trafficking, and hustling. It's vampirism with a ski mask on and not a drop of pretentiousness. This is business, but when you work hard, you also play hard. <br /> <br /> As far as infrastructure, I'm still working it out. I have Miami as the headquarters because in the corebook, iirc, they reference that the CS actually started in Miami. I think this fits well, with the port of Miami and just all the general hedonism and traffic that goes on there. It's a flashy place and an aesthetic backdrop for a new and chic organization. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27842-shovelheart3","name":"ShovelHeart3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27842_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T11:44:07-07:00","id":1514032,"title":"","content":"I'm confused. What is this... sect? Where is it mentioned? <br /> <br /> For me, while I like the focus on smaller cults, the whole nuCamarilla thing is a non-starter. A system that began in the early-modern period to deal with modern problems and which has numerous supernaturally talented minds leading it does not do a 180 at an expected problem and end up like whatever it is in V5. I like my secular, global, hands-off yet inescapable Camarilla. If a cult can survive in that environment, props to them, if the Camarilla needed to be hit with the idiot stick to allow such a thing... no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T23:36:53-07:00","id":1514083,"title":"","content":"Not really a &quot;Sect&quot; per se<br /> <br /> <b>The Circulatory System</b> is an international human trafficking network that smuggles important vessels between domains and chronicles the powers of the blood vintages they move.<br /> Vampires take advantage of the Circulatory System illegal services to obtain blood with a specific resonance from selected vessels. The Circulatory System is an exploitive network and cares little for the long-term well-being of their vessels, beyond the dip in profits the traffickers suffer when such kine die prematurely. Many Kindred can look past such minor issues to the pioneering studies the System makes possible by unlocking new and valuable features of the Blood.<br /> <br /> It is a lore sheet thing, from Vampire: The Masquerade 5th Edition Corebook, p. 386 \u200b, representing a character with a connection to the Circulatory System (as a client, trafficker, or former mortal vessel turned vampire, etc)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T00:33:00-07:00","id":1514090,"title":"","content":"Honestly, sounds like too much hassle and risk, and I don't think a prince would appreciate the effects it would have on stability. Much better to control and embezzle from a couple of legal local businesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T05:10:40-07:00","id":1514107,"title":"","content":"I mean, even as a \u201cpseudo-sect\u201d, it\u2019s not particularly much different to, say, the Amici Noctis, an organization that bridges the sects. It\u2019s still just an organization of blood smugglers, nothing philosophical or unlife-defining about it. <br /> <br /> The Camarilla is a Sect because it has a defined and self-contained philosophy as to the way a vampire should interact with mortals and the world; that you must uphold the Masquerade, that the Traditions are what allow vampires to flourish and cooperate as a group. <br /> The Sabbat is a Sect because it has a diametrically opposed philosophy that cannot be simultaneously followed by a Camarilla-aligned Vampire. They reject the Masquerade and Traditions, they believe that the Cainite is inherently superior to the kine and should not be ashamed of this fact, that Cainite cooperation should be ingrained through the Vaulderie and devotion to Caine. <br /> Both inherently define a vampires attitudes to the world at large, and do so in contradictory ways such that a Vampire cannot be simultaneously following both. <br /> <br /> What defines the Circulatory System beyond \u201csell blood get money\u201d? What makes it so that a vampire belongs to the Circulatory Club without simultaneously being able to hold Camarilla or Sabbat membership?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27967-caerolion","name":"Caerolion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T10:37:56-07:00","id":1514118,"title":"","content":"It just sounds implausible to me. <br /> I get what they're doing, bringing attention to human trafficking. But if you were sincere you'd probably take a more mature path. This just seems like kids thinking of things edgy and evil for shock value, as is the whole ressonance system (Wow cool I got a +1 bonus from drinking from victim of child abuse! Maybe I should abuse more children for a tastier herd!) <br /> <br /> On one hand we have a smartly satirical setting about wealthy parasites literally draining the masses beneath them while trying to get a leg up on one another, and on the other we've got people greatly risking their unlives and grand world-spanning conspiracy because they enjoy playing with their food. First edition had a few whacky ideas but at least they were all-in on the core concept, the themes, and presented vampires as something that could conceivably hold up a masquerade. I feel like we're witnessing punk rock transitioning to emo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T20:13:34-07:00","id":1514155,"title":"","content":"Good grief, are some of you really this hung up on terminology? One of the literal definitions of the word &quot;sect&quot; is &quot;a faction united by common interests or beliefs&quot; and it's not even enough for that I use the term &quot;pseudosect&quot;, lmao.<br /> <br /> I've already given several ideas on how to flesh out the identity of the organization. And that's what it is, an organization. It's bigger than a cult. It has a reason for being.<br /> <br /> The Anarch sect boils down to &quot;fuck the Camarilla and the Sabbat&quot;. The Camarilla's boils down to &quot;we want to hold power and this is the system we use for that goal&quot;. All the Sects started as a mere reaction to something: The Camarilla to the Inquisition and the Sabbat and Anarchs to the Camarilla. The meaning came post hoc and complexity does in fact emerge from simplicity. So, if you can't brainstorm interesting stories, philosophies, characters and concepts for this very modern idea, perhaps that's a call to examine the effectiveness of your own imaginations? Do you really need your hands held that much?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a><br /> You're the one projecting edginess. The Circulatory System is about Blood, the most fundamental thing to a vampire's existence. It is unpretentious by its very nature. If you can't see the importance of that beyond your own juvenile reductionism, that's a deficiency on your part. You also have to seem to have no clue about the practical utility of the CS. Oh, it's easier just to embezzle blood? What if a Tremere needs a rare type for a Ritual? What if you have a Ventrue with extremely particular taste? Your argument is like saying &quot;well, I have a national forest in my backyard, why don't I just go gather some food instead of going to the grocery store?&quot; Because the grocery store offers variety, convenience and also very importantly, safety. My own Nagaraja character is going to hunt Vampires, Hunters and Werewolves for their blood. Yeah, good luck &quot;embezzling&quot; Garou vitae, king. You also grossly overlook the utility it provides given all the new mechanics and properties of vitae in V5.<br /> <br /> And another thing I don't get is this obsession with exclusivity. Why can't a Tremere be both in the Cam and the CS? Both serve their goals. Why can't someone in the Anarchs be in the CS, as well? It provides a utility I doubt most would want to pass up. You all realize people do typically hold jobs in addition to their personal politics, right? The CS doesn't have to be some closed door society. It's the exact opposite, which is what makes it interesting. VTM finally has a space for conflicting ideals to coexist at a broad level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27842,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27842-shovelheart3","user":"ShovelHeart3","date":". 06-07-2023, 11:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27842-shovelheart3","name":"ShovelHeart3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27842_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T23:31:25-07:00","id":1514168,"title":"","content":"Can I have some of that salt on my poppcorn?<br /> Look, it is a discussion<br /> As you wrote, you like the idea of the Circulatory System and have your ideas to mold it in to a sect-like thing.<br /> Thats okay. Go for it! By all means<br /> But you wrote this because wanted opinions, ideas, criticism, or wanted an echo chamber for your own thoughts and a pat on your head how good idea it was?<br /> It really wasn't<br /> A sect is a social organization of vampires, usually composed of multiple clans that form a league or compact. Each sect has a dogma and an objective its members seek to attain.<br /> Yes, terminology matters to many - to others, not that much<br /> The <b>Camarilla</b>, the <b>Sabbat</b>, the <b>Anarch Movement </b>(heck even the materiels describe, the Anarchs themselves are <i>not a sect</i>, per se; in most areas, they were regarded as merely a faction on the fringes of the dominant Camarilla hierarchy) the <b>Ashirra</b> are both &quot;teens&quot;, in the eyes of a sufficiently old (~500 years behinds it back) vampire, nothing more than a Cainite fad (and if you want, you can toss in the mix the <b>Nepthali </b>from Gehenna)<br /> The<b> Laibon Legacies of the Ebony Kingdom</b> or the<b> Einherjar of Skandinavia </b>even the the<b> Raktasadhu of India</b> are old as dirt, like the <b>Tal'Mahe'Ra </b>and the <b>Inconnu </b>(this one more or less)<br /> Nothing prevents you to treat the <b>Circulatory System </b>as a Sect or form it in to one, or even just a workable vampire organization<br /> We just pointed out, in an usual setting, the Circulatory System <i>why wouldn't work</i><br /> Feel free to not agree with those opinions<br /> They are just that<br /> Opinions and suggestions<br /> As you said, the Vampires are dependent of blood... thus it is very risky to depend on such an organization<br /> But this is just our.. suggestion and opinion, why wouldn't work<br /> You are free to not agree with it\u200b<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T00:49:38-07:00","id":1514173,"title":"","content":"<br /> A vampire worth his salt should have nailed down a safe and sustainable stratagem for hunting, be it seducing horny club goers, feeding from the sleeping, house calls, or something of that nature. The occasional drunk mugging or homeless assault can be sustainable in some territories. If you can't make a good strat, you are a liability, you should die and your sire made a mistake embracing you. Vampires are a society entirely populated by people who hunt and the most valued thing politically is hunting grounds. Sure, they pretend not to be hunters, but you're not going to get any respect if you aren't self sufficient in getting human blood. Nobody should need it, and the people who need it shouldn't really have the capabilities to afford it. A Ventrue with very specific blood needs or a Tremere who &quot;needs&quot; a specific type of blood both has the support of their clan and should have the resources and acumen to arrange for their own procurement. <br /> <br /> The more people involved in a crime the more likely you'll get in trouble for it. Assault might be a more dangerous strat than the other options but the individual nature of the process keeps it miles better than a sophisticated international people-smuggling ring. There are just too many points of failure and too much reliance on others. <br /> <br /> And yeah, It's incredibly pretentious. You're making massive masquerade risks, risks against yourself, violating humans in one of the worst ways possible, and risking how many accomplices... for better tasting food. It's edgy bullshit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T02:10:21-07:00","id":1514176,"title":"","content":"I'm not against the idea of being able to purchase blood and dolls without hunting for yourself, or having vampires who profit off of trafficking cooperating with other vampires and their traffickers to create a larger international ring. Personally, I would put the stipulation that they they're the behind the scenes profiting from the crimes of mortals, and the trafficking group is a human set up, as it's important to me that humanity gets to own its own fuck ups not have them absolved by conveniently handing them off to supernatural predators; it's boring, and also a gigantic criminal syndicate where vampires are very heavily involved is firing a signal flare for hunter attention.<br /> So in my opinion, like the Inquisition, the Circulatory System should be a loose cooperation between disparate groups, not an actual organisation in and of itself.<br /> <br /> As for clan makeup; If specific clans need to meddle in trafficking to get specific blood - particularly financially rich, socially structured clans with the requisite disciplines like the Ventrue and Tremere - they will have set up their own circles of kidnappers loyal to themselves. These can be cooperate with others, but they don't need them.<br /> The Hecata need this least of any clan. They don't need the blood dolls or the profit from getting involved because they have both in their massive herd of insanely rich 1% mortal relatives/cult members (and the non-Giovanni are a handful of vamps without much presence at the moment, so they're not much of a factor on this discussion). Their chief resonance is Null, nothing, nada, corpses. They've already got their niche nailed; it's being the vampire ghostbusters and the Bank. You may argue that the Putanesca, as the actual criminal syndicate branch of a Clan whose reputation for such is overblown, could be involved - but the Putanesca were a mistake who should never have been written into the game in the first place and I'm not - and shall not be - factoring them in. Besides, the involvement of some Putanesca would be a drop of Hecata influence in a sea of other clans.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, crime and violation like trafficking combined with blood sorcery and &quot;I can get you<i> anything </i>you need, my friend&quot; while offering its services with no bias towards Clan or Sect is very much the Setite niche. Ministry, whatever. As far as I'm concerned this is their turf and the other clans are just playing on their playground by their permission. Involvement from others (particularly the other independents) would be individuals, not Clans as a whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T03:54:52-07:00","id":1514180,"title":"","content":"Thinking on it, it could work as a network better beyond just blood. Say they also provide mobility for other stuff-say vampire specific items and vampires themselves. Blood being just one front in a larger psuado crime syndicate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T04:12:31-07:00","id":1514181,"title":"","content":"Dude, you created a topic titled \u201cThe New Sect\u201d, in regards to a game where Sect already has strong definitions, and are surprised that people are judging your idea around those criteria as opposed to a definition the game itself? A Clan has definitions beyond the terminology in VtM, but if you post a topic about a new Clan you\u2019ve homebrewed, people are going to compare it to the other Clans as VtM defines it, as opposed to the dictionary definition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27967-caerolion","name":"Caerolion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T10:03:14-07:00","id":1514201,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> <br /> You literally did not address a single one of my points. Let's go over this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509436-the-new-sect?p=1514173#post1514173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A vampire worth his salt should have nailed down a safe and sustainable stratagem for hunting, be it seducing horny club goers, feeding from the sleeping, house calls, or something of that nature. The occasional drunk mugging or homeless assault can be sustainable in some territories. If you can't make a good strat, you are a liability, you should die and your sire made a mistake embracing you. Vampires are a society entirely populated by people who hunt and the most valued thing politically is hunting grounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>And hunting can be unsafe, inconvenient or simply incapable of supplying what you need, easily, or even at all. This goes back to the grocery store metaphor, which you completely ignored because it's inconvenient to your non-existent argument. What if you're an impotent lick or a Thin-Blood and all the hunting grounds are taken? Boy, I bet you wish there was some organization that could just sell you what you need.....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bA Ventrue with very specific blood needs or a Tremere who &quot;needs&quot; a specific type of blood both has the support of their clan and should have the resources and acumen to arrange for their own procurement. </div> </div> </div>That then means that they have to rely on someone within their clan. What if they're in low standing? What if they need discretion? There's a million contextual reasons why they may want to use a third-party, all of which you carelessly give no consideration to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The more people involved in a crime the more likely you'll get in trouble for it. Assault might be a more dangerous strat than the other options but the individual nature of the process keeps it miles better than a sophisticated international people-smuggling ring. There are just too many points of failure and too much reliance on others. </div> </div> </div>Your argument is that a covert operation is too risky, so it's better for thousands of Kindred to be out there hunting night in and night out, with all kinds of risks and exposures involved, especially when the SI will be looking for such behavior? Your rationale is that it's more lowkey to randomly commit a million crimes in public than to covertly supply them in relative secrecy? That's interesting. And you also say there's too much reliance on others, immediately after saying that you should rely on your Clan to pander to you. That makes no sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're making massive masquerade risks, risks against yourself, violating humans in one of the worst ways possible, and risking how many accomplices... for better tasting food. </div> </div> </div>Right, because harvesting blood in secrecy is far more of a Masquerade threat than some Brujah having a bad night hunting and flipping his shit on the street. And you also don't take the new blood mechanics into account, which are important. And better tasting food is going to sate the Beast more and be more effective at staving it off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yeah, It's incredibly pretentious. It's edgy bullshit. </div> </div> </div>But enough about your posting. You talk a lot of shit without actually giving any qualitative arguments; rather, you repeatedly contradict your own arguments and ignore anything that is inconvenient to your narrative, especially context. You even call the CS &quot;edgy&quot; after going on a tirade about Vampiric Social Darwinism, lmao - nice self awareness. And Humanity is central to the core of VTM. Buying blood, especially different types of blood can help you circumvent Humanity degradation, especially if you need a Dyscrasia that can only be obtained through negative experience.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27967-caerolion\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27967\" data-vbnamecard=\"27967\">Caerolion</a> <br /> Let's do a little Vampiric math:<br /> You have a broad collection of vampires, bigger than a cult<br /> +<br /> An ethos for being (profit and power)<br /> +<br /> \u200bAn opportunity to develop an internal culture around the aggregate of Clans within and the activities associated with it<br /> <br /> =<br /> What? What would you say that would equal? Might you say it's a &quot;pseudosect&quot;? That's why the whole kvetching over this terminology is ridiculous. It makes you look like you're being willfully obstinate or unwilling to think of anything that is novel in comparison to the established lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27842-shovelheart3","name":"ShovelHeart3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27842_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T11:03:26-07:00","id":1514206,"title":"","content":"What points did you actually make?<br /> <br /> If you don't have a hunting ground, you probably don't have much in the way of income and will have significantly less in terms of political power. What rights do you have to millionaire food delivery? If you're a fledgling with limited access to information, can you even find the highly secretive group of traffickers?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That then means that they have to rely on someone within their clan. What if they're in low standing? What if they need discretion? There's a million contextual reasons why they may want to use a third-party, all of which you carelessly give no consideration to. </div> </div> </div> Of course I fucking won't give any consideration. If you're a Ventrue or Tremere and somehow fucked up enough to not get any investment from your seniors who almost certainly vetted you as a potential asset before the embrace, then you've done an amazing job and should probably consider making a new character. I don't think you understand these clans. Childer are an investment, the childer know this, and there's no problem having debts in these very close knit clans. Somethings that you also seem to avoid acknowledging is that 1: Ventrue with rarefied feeding types are great investments because they're easy to control and most egregiously 2: That your example with the Tremere isn't a need, it's a want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your argument is that a covert operation is too risky, so it's better for thousands of Kindred to be out there hunting night in and night out, with all kinds of risks and exposures involved, especially when the SI will be looking for such behavior? Your rationale is that it's more lowkey to randomly commit a million crimes in public than to covertly supply them in relative secrecy? That's interesting. And you also say there's too much reliance on others, immediately after saying that you should rely on your Clan to pander to you. That makes no sense. </div> </div> </div>That makes plenty sense. The local members of your clan are LITERALLY YOUR FAMILY. Sire, child, neonate... these aren't coincidental terms. If you can't lean on family a little, what even is the point? On the otherhand, an organization of human traffickers? Like, I realise vampires might often form less than ideal family relationships but I'd take dysfunctional family over strangers who sell slaves for a living.<br /> <br /> Oh and I almost skipped over it: What do you mean to sarcastically say &quot;A covert operation is too risky so it's better.... commit thousands a million crimes in public.&quot;<br /> Yes. A million small crimes is better than a human trafficking ring. Have you ever gotten a bike stolen? Police will do all the work of adding it as a statistic, even if it was a really nice bike, but a trafficking ring? Call the Feds! I don't understand why you're so willfully ignoring the logistics of the situation. A cassanova just needs a party place and a private place, in modern times she can use an app; a sandman can optimize his hunts by getting keys to the places he visits, and if someone assaults a drunk, junkie or hobo will the police be called and if so how long will they take to get there? Ultimately, the only person responsible for doing this right is the vampire.<br /> <br /> Now for a transnational blood smuggling operation. Fuck me I can't believe I need to explain where this can go wrong.<br /> 1- You need to abduct people, sometimes very specific people who aren't easy to take. That can go wrong. Everything on this list can go wrong<br /> 2- You need to transport these people without getting caught or allowing any escapes. With some rare types, there's going to be long distances involved.<br /> 3- You need to hold these people without getting caught. You also need to keep them fed<br /> 4- You need to facilitate communications between clients, kidnappers, and other kidnappers.<br /> 6- You'll need to control a large number of amoral thugs and every single one of them is a liability.<br /> 7- All parties need to avoid the possibility of being blackmailed<br /> 8- Vampires are very prone to sabotaging one another and selling to vampire X can invite danger from vampire Y who isn't so dependent on the system<br /> 9- The once-a-blue-moon feeding going wrong might attract hunters but that's nothing compared to literal-fucking-abductions<br /> 10- In case it needs to be said but if one person goes down here there's a very good chance that other people will go down.<br /> <br /> There's just far, far, far too many people in a supply chain. Far to many weak potential weak links and external enemies.<br /> Oh, one last thing, let's talk about scale here. SCALE. Let's say a vampire takes one blood point per night. A human needs like two months to properly recover blood cells and the like. So if you want to keep the humans at peak delicious you'll need like sixty people per vampire. Yeah, I'll take my chances with the Brujah.<br /> <br /> Nail.In.The.Coffin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You even call the CS &quot;edgy&quot; after going on a tirade about Vampiric Social Darwinism, </div> </div> </div>My Brother in Christ<br /> Did you read the Memo<br /> <br /> WE ARE TALKING ABOUT VAMPIRES.<br /> SEXY BLOODSUCKING DEMONS OF THE NIGHT<br /> METAPHORS FOR A PARASITIC ARISTOCRACY<br /> <br /> We can allow them a <i>little</i> edge. It just needs to make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T11:34:08-07:00","id":1514213,"title":"","content":"No he's right a massive trade network of blood exchange is inherently more risky than being a succesful hunter. I'm unclear why you think it wouldn't be. The fact it is a massive potential breach is actually an interesting plot point if you wanted to run this sect, they'd have to dedicate a lot of logistics to hiding an industrialised pan national and it could be the source of a lot of interesting stories.<br /> <br /> Also the way you're arguing back implies you think it's a good idea rather than being a cool idea for in game-is that the case?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-08-2023, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T12:13:49-07:00","id":1514221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509436-the-new-sect?p=1514213#post1514213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No he's right a massive trade network of blood exchange is inherently more risky than being a successful hunter. I'm unclear why you think it wouldn't be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it depends on context, which means he's only partially there. You can easily spot someone bighting into a neck on some nightclub's CCTV. You also have the issue of possible public frenzy, Nosferatu, Brujah, Malkavian, Toreador drama and so on and so forth. Think of all the things that could go wrong in public, especially with how pervasive public surveillance is these days. The SI is familiar with how vampires hunt. They know about the dark corners, racks, clubs and so on. I don't think some of you guys really take into account the gravity of technology in 2023 when you imply public hunting is some low risk thing. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The fact it is a massive potential breach is actually an interesting plot point if you wanted to run this sect, they'd have to dedicate a lot of logistics to hiding an industrialised pan national and it could be the source of a lot of interesting stories. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think so. It's a different angle of addressing the Masquerade. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also the way you're arguing back implies you think it's a good idea rather than being a cool idea for in game-is that the case? </div> </div> </div>I think it's a matter of both. Yes, it may sometimes be easier to hunt, but you have to think of the CS as a premium service. Perhaps someone is too busy to hunt? Perhaps you need something special and don't have the time or resources to track it down? Perhaps you have an enemy you'd like to avoid crossing paths with? The truth is that vampires NEED blood. The CS is yet another avenue to attain it. I never said it's risk free, after all, I did equate it to a criminal organization, but the thing I don't understand is how the practical utility isn't more apparent, especially with the new vitae mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27842-shovelheart3","name":"ShovelHeart3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27842_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T12:34:25-07:00","id":1514225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShovelHeart3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509436-the-new-sect?p=1514221#post1514221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it depends on context, which means he's only partially there. You can easily spot someone bighting into a neck on some nightclub's CCTV. You also have the issue of possible public frenzy, Nosferatu, Brujah, Malkavian, Toreador drama and so on and so forth. Think of all the things that could go wrong in public, especially with how pervasive public surveillance is these days. The SI is familiar with how vampires hunt. They know about the dark corners, racks, clubs and so on. I don't think some of you guys really take into account the gravity of technology in 2023 when you imply public hunting is some low risk thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, I think so. It's a different angle of addressing the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think it's a matter of both. Yes, it may sometimes be easier to hunt, but you have to think of the CS as a premium service. Perhaps someone is too busy to hunt? Perhaps you need something special and don't have the time or resources to track it down? Perhaps you have an enemy you'd like to avoid crossing paths with? The truth is that vampires NEED blood. The CS is yet another avenue to attain it. I never said it's risk free, after all, I did equate it to a criminal organization, but the thing I don't understand is how the practical utility isn't more apparent, especially with the new vitae mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and a massive crime network as you describe it is going to be far easy to catch onto that, the moment the 2nd inquisition catches onto it,it's going to be far easier to mess with than your guy in a night club especially if you're taking such a hard stance on modern tech surveillance.<br /> <br /> it doesn't really addres the masquarade, its a massive risk to it. Thats a cool plot point.<br /> <br /> it sounds more like a niche indulgence than a practical service. I can see it working as part of niche requests for blood like ventrue or a sabbat blood orgy but logistically as a large scale institution it doesn't seem more practical than conventional hunting and has a lot of supplementary risks built in. I'd back it up with other firms of trade such as arms, cross city transportation and other vampiric concerns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T12:35:13-07:00","id":1514226,"title":"","content":"Double post <br /> This site's way too sensitive with the spam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 06-13-2023, 03:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T12:47:32-07:00","id":1514228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509436-the-new-sect?p=1514225#post1514225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes and a massive crime network as you describe it is going to be far easy to catch onto that</div> </div> </div> </div>Like how they've already caught onto the Camarilla, the Anarchs and the Sabbat?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the moment the 2nd inquisition catches onto it,it's going to be far easier to mess with than your guy in a night club especially if you're taking such a hard stance on modern tech surveillance. </div> </div> </div>Really, because something I would do as SI would be to put agents in nightclubs and wait for blankbodies to lure them somewhere or develop a relationship, which I could then turn into an ambush. If I were SI, nightclubs would be where I put heavy presence because you're factually going to catch a lot there. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it doesn't really addres the masquarade, its a massive risk to it. Thats a cool plot point. </div> </div> </div>Yes, it does. It has to do business in a manner which preserves and respects the Masquerade or it wouldn't fly at all. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it sounds more like a niche indulgence than a practical service. I can see it working as part of niche requests for blood like ventrue or a sabbat blood orgy but logistically as a large scale institution it doesn't seem more practical than conventional hunting and has a lot of supplementary risks built in. I'd back it up with other firms of trade such as arms, cross city transportation and other vampiric concerns. </div> </div> </div>Again, how niche or indulgent it is depends on the context. You have to use context. If you're a neonate and everyone owns every piece of turf around, how are you going to get fed? You basically have to take what you can get and that may not be very beneficial to you. I think you guys have been making feeding a bit too much of a reflexive thing and not fully considering all the potential difficulties that can go along with it. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27842-shovelheart3","name":"ShovelHeart3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27842_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T13:25:15-07:00","id":1514236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShovelHeart3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509436-the-new-sect?p=1514228#post1514228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like how they've already caught onto the Camarilla, the Anarchs and the Sabbat?<br /> <br /> <br /> Really, because something I would do as SI would be to put agents in nightclubs and wait for blankbodies to lure them somewhere or develop a relationship, which I could then turn into an ambush. If I were SI, nightclubs would be where I put heavy presence because you're factually going to catch a lot there.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, it does. It has to do business in a manner which preserves and respects the Masquerade or it wouldn't fly at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> Again, how niche or indulgent it is depends on the context. You have to use context. If you're a neonate and everyone owns every piece of turf around, how are you going to get fed? You basically have to take what you can get and that may not be very beneficial to you. I think you guys have been making feeding a bit too much of a reflexive thing and not fully considering all the potential difficulties that can go along with it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes exactly. Except it'll be a lot easier to pull apart because it's a highly interconnected network. Even better I get to harm other vampires with the economic fallout when I cut one section of the supply chain. Now I've got a load of rusty feeders pouring into the city as they panic.<br /> <br /> I'd do both. But i know id have an easier time with a pan national crime syndicate since I don't have to pack nightclubs in extended stake outs on assumption a vampire might show up.<br /> <br /> then it's not going to fly as you're describing it since it's far more suspectable to masquarade breach but like I said that's an interesting plot point.<br /> <br /> The average neonate is not going to have the resources to make it worth this sects time. You're risking you're wellfare, resources and time for this. How much do you think they're going to charge for this service?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-09-2023, 02:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T14:10:05-07:00","id":1514239,"title":"","content":"I think the basic idea of vampires running some kind of underground criminal blood-slave network is fine. It makes sense for the setting. And some version of it has been around forever - even the first edition corebook's section on Gary, IN as a setting mentioned the ghoul Williams and his &quot;auction&quot; that sells kidnapped victims to be used as vessels to the area's vampires.<br /> <br /> The Circulatory System is simply a more developed version of this idea. There are human trafficking organizations even today in the most modern countries. Until the people reach their final destinations and find out they are not sold to a brothel or sweatshop, it'll just seem like any other human trafficking organization. In fact, they can even be used in that capacity UNTIL some vampire makes the final purchase. Or it could even involve a cover in more legitimate organizations. It could be a modelling service, travel nurse program, migrant farm labor, a temp agency that covers a specific kind of employee like the hospitality service, or something else. All that is needed is something that attracts people to want to move for a job and perhaps put up in corporate dormitory to allow for surveillance. Then you just need to be judicious on who is selected to be the meal while not jeopardizing the network as a whole. So if law enforcement does uncover parts of the organization, it could appear perfectly &quot;normal&quot; though criminal. It no more uncovers the existence of vampires than exposure of actual human trafficking organizations in the real world does.<br /> <br /> If done well, I don't think it is any increased danger to the Masquerade to any other of the activities of vampires in the setting. I have not read any actual information on the Circulatory System so I don't know if it is not implemented well in practice. But I think the general idea can work (just as much as anything else), and an ST can always make adjustments as needed so it fits their particular vision of the setting. <br /> <br /> But if the ST wants, of course something could happen which does produce a risk to the Masquerade just like anytime a vampire does something it might lead to someone figuring out the truth. Maybe a mistake was made. Or maybe it was implemented in some incompetent fashion. If that makes a good plot for an ST, those options work too.<br /> <br /> Now I don't see this as a &quot;sect&quot; like how we talk about the Camarilla, Sabbat, or Inconnu. But there can be plenty of organizations within the Camarilla similar to this. Or one of the Revenant families may do the same thing for the Sabbat. Or one of the Independent clans runs a similar organization for their own needs, or to build business with the other sects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T05:48:57-07:00","id":1515853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509436-the-new-sect?p=1510411#post1510411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed Ragged Robin. The Tremere clan won't leave the Camarilla as that sect benefits them the most and at best you might get a few rebellious ones who might want to join and get on the ground floor and hope for positions of importance.</div> </div> </div> </div>But on the other hand, House Carna could use that as a trampoline to power, leaving Anarch Rabble behind. Who wouldn't be tempted by the promise of cracking the mystery of thin-blood vitae...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27765-euderos","name":"Euderos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27765_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}